## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop:** `game` state object; `mulberry32(seed)` used for all rng calls; `endTurn()` calls updateProduction→updateColonists→updateCooldowns→checkAshstorm→updateTrade→fireEvent in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map:** 8x8 `this.map` built with `this.rng()`; `canBuild()` checks `tile.terrain !== btype.terrain`; `calcAdjacencyBonus()` feeds `b.productivity`, read in `updateProduction()`. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy:** storage caps/overflow enforced in `updateProduction()`; but only shallow chain (greenhouse subtracts a flat `waterUsed` constant, forge/refinery consume no inputs) — no real ore→metal/multi-resource transform. Score 1.

**F4 — Population:** colonist records have skill/fatigue/morale/assigned; `c.skillLevel` read in `updateProduction()` skillBonus calc, but `fatigue` is never read directly by production, only indirectly via morale. Score 1.

**F5 — Needs:** `produced.food/water -= popConsumption` each turn; `handleShortage()` cuts morale; `moraleMult` scales productivity in `updateProduction()`; idle colonists recover morale/fatigue. Score 2.

**F6 — Research:** 8 nodes in `this.research`; `canResearch()` enforces prereq; `doResearch()` deducts cost; but `power_1`, `labor_1`, `automation` have no code effect anywhere (only farming_1/mining_1/water_1/storm_1/storage_1 are read). Score 1.

**F7 — Events:** 10 entries in `eventDeck`; weighted pick in `fireEvent()`; cooldown map decremented in `updateCooldowns()`; only 3 events (`trade_opportunity`, `labor_strike`, `research_insight`) have `choices`, short of required 4+. Score 1.

**F8 — Trade:** `caravanPrices` computed from `globalDemand` (drifts via rng) and `playerStock`; `caravanInventory` capped/limited; `tradeWithCaravan()` handles both buy/sell, wired to click handlers in `renderTrade()`. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard:** `checkAshstorm()` fires periodically, `severity` grows with `this.turn`; damages `b.health`; `updateProduction()` scales productivity by `b.health/100`; `storm_1` research and `shelter` building reduce damage; `repairBuilding()` costs parts and restores health. Score 2.

**F10 — Save/load:** `saveToTextarea()` dumps full JSON state to textarea; `loadFromTextarea()` parses with try/catch and `alert()`s on parse failure, but does no schema validation of loaded fields. Score 1.

**F11 — End conditions:** win check in `endTurn()` (turn/pop/resources); lose check in `updateColonists()` when `colonists.length===0`; `endGame()` computes score from pop/research/resources/turn and renders `#end-game-modal`. Score 2.

**F12 — UI:** tab click listeners wired; `logEvent` stores `turn`, rendered as `T${entry.turn}`; tile tooltips show health/bonus source; keydown handler for Space and digit-key tab shortcuts; media queries at 768px/480px. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel:** `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, ranges, prereqs, exclusive assignment); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 turns calling core functions directly (no render calls in loop) and prints `computeStateHash()`. Score 2.

**G1:** `researchDone.has('farming_1')`/`'mining_1'` checked as hardcoded special-cases inside `updateProduction()` building loop, bonus added to `produced.food`/`metal`. Score 2.

**G2:** `handleShortage()` cuts `c.morale` on food/water deficit → `avgMorale` recomputed in `updateColonists()` → `moraleMult` scales productivity in `updateProduction()` every turn. Score 4.

**G3:** `checkAshstorm()` cuts `b.health` → `updateProduction()` scales productivity by `b.health/100` → `repairBuilding()` spends `parts`, restores `b.health=100`. Score 4.

**G4:** `caravanPrices[res] = basePrices*globalDemand[res]*stockFactor` where `stockFactor` derived from `this.resources[res]`; `globalDemand` drifts via rng each caravan visit. Score 4.

**G5:** `labor_strike` choices both mutate morale differently; `trade_opportunity`/`research_insight` mutate on accept but no-op on decline. Score 3.

